## Summary

**Root cause fix**: `StatusBanner.tsx` had a `setTimeout` callback that force-cast `window` to a type claiming `__APP_CONFIG__: { buildId: string }` exists, then unconditionally read `config.buildId`. Since no code anywhere sets `window.__APP_CONFIG__`, the value is `undefined` at runtime, and `.buildId` throws. I changed the type assertion to mark `__APP_CONFIG__` as optional (reflecting reality) and added a guard (`if (config)`) so the log only runs when the config actually exists — matching how `handleRefresh`'s similarly-unsafe cast should have been handled, but keeping the diff minimal and scoped to the actual bug.

**Regression test**: Added `frontend/tests/status-banner.spec.ts`, a Playwright spec consistent with the existing e2e test suite conventions (`tests/login.spec.ts`). It navigates to `/login`, listens for `pageerror` events, waits >1.5s (past the `setTimeout` delay), and asserts no page errors occurred. This reproduces the exact bug scenario end-to-end.

**Environment limitations encountered while validating**: This sandbox cannot fully execute the project's own `npm test` (`bunx playwright test`):
- `bun` is not installed (only `npx` is available).
- Node is v20.9.0, but `vite@8` (via `rolldown`) requires Node ≥20.19/22.12 (`node:util` `styleText` export missing) — so the Vite dev server that Playwright's `webServer` needs cannot start at all, even for the new spec.
- `dotenv` (imported by `playwright.config.ts`/`tests/config.ts`) isn't declared in `frontend/package.json` devDependencies at all — a pre-existing gap I worked around locally (`npm install --no-save dotenv`, not persisted) just to get `tsc`/`biome` tooling working; I did not "fix" this since it's unrelated to the bug and out of scope.
- The other existing specs also require a live Supabase-backed backend and real credentials, which aren't available here.

These are pre-existing infra issues unrelated to my change (verified with `git stash`). To still validate correctness, I wrote an isolated Node reproduction (`/tmp/opencode/repro.mjs`) mirroring the exact callback logic: it confirms the pre-fix code throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'buildId')` and the post-fix code does not. I also ran `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json` (the same typecheck `npm run build` uses) — passes clean before and after. `biome check` on the touched lines is clean; the tool flags pre-existing formatting issues elsewhere in the file/repo that I did not touch and did not introduce.

